• packages/components/src/globals/scss/components/list/_list.scss: this is where the core ordered-list styles live. It contains the rule

  .bx--list--ordered:not(.bx--list--nested) {
    counter-reset: item;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .bx--list--ordered:not(.bx--list--nested) > .bx--list__item::before {
    content: counter(item) ". ";
    counter-increment: item;
    /* … */
  }

  Removing or disabling the `counter-reset` here is the only way to fix Firefox numbering today, so we need to wrap that block in a selector guard for the new `.bx--list--native` class (e.g. `:not(.bx--list--native)`).

• packages/react/src/components/OrderedList/OrderedList.js: this component already reads the `useNativeStyles` prop and adds `bx--list--native` to the top-level `<ol>`, but because the stylesheet has no special rules for `.bx--list--native`, the override never kicks in. We need to make sure the prop is passed and then ensure the CSS file recognizes that class and disables the counter.

• packages/react/src/components/OrderedList/OrderedList.mdx: update the documentation so that we show how to use the new `useNativeStyles` prop and explain that it enables the browser’s native decimal list styling instead of Carbon’s pseudo-element counters.
